hexagon: an F16 SwiGLU output for its only reader, an HMX MUL_MAT

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The HMX MUL_MAT converts its F32 activation to F16 before the multiply. In
the FFN block of Qwen3.5, ffn_down is the only reader of the SwiGLU output.
The GLU op writes that tensor as F32, and ffn_down reads it and converts
each value to F16. With this patch the two ops move an F16 tensor, half the
bytes:
  - ggml_hexagon_mm_fusion_plan (htp-mm-fusion.h) finds each SwiGLU op
    whose only reader is a MUL_MAT on the HMX 2D path. It gives the two op
    nodes an F16 view of the output tensor, with the same data and buffer.
  - The GLU op (act-ops.c) writes the F16 rows. It converts each VTCM row
    with hvx_vec_f32_to_f16, the conversion of the HMX activation load.
    Thus each value gets the F16 bits that the MUL_MAT makes from the F32
    value, also a value outside the F16 range.
  - hmx_mm_op_matmul (matmul-ops.c) reads an F16 src1 on the HMX 2D path.
    The DMA moves the F16 rows into VTCM, and HVX puts them into the
    activation tiles in the lane order of the F32 path.
  - try_fuse_mul_mat_add keeps the F16 view as the src1 of the fused
    MUL_MAT_ADD, and it computes the kernel params from the F32 tensor.
The switch GGML_HEXAGON_FUSE_F16_ACT: 1 is the preset value, 0 disables
the plan.

test-backend-ops gets the case FFN_SWIGLU: the FFN block of Qwen3.5 on a
whole graph (the norm, the gate and the up MUL_MAT, the SwiGLU, the down
MUL_MAT and the residual ADD), with the HVX and the HMX shapes and the 4B
shapes.

The tests on the host:
  - The lab target f16act (hexagon-sim v79, functional): the GLU op with
    an F16 dst against the F32 dst and the conversion, and MUL_MAT (+ADD)
    with an F16 src1 against the F32 src1, also with values outside the
    F16 range. 8 cases, 0 differences.
  - hexhost_graphs (the fake DSP) on the 2B and the 4B: decode, decode
    with 4 state snapshots, prefill 512 and 1024, the MTP draft and the
    image turn at 576 and 768 tokens, with the F16 cache and with the Q8_0
    cache and flash attention, each with the plan on and off (56 runs).
    Each run passes, and the supports_op decisions and the DSP ops of on
    and off are the same. The 4B prefill of 1024 tokens has 32 plans.

The tests on the phone (HTP0, v79, the 4B Q8_0), the plan on against
GGML_HEXAGON_FUSE_F16_ACT=0:
  - ffncheck: the same hashes and non-finite counts in all 18 cases,
    among them the cases with values outside the F16 range.
  - test-backend-ops FFN_SWIGLU: 70/70.
  - llama-perplexity -b 1 (the decode path), two runs of each: the same KL
    numbers in the four runs (mean KLD 0.000557).
  - llama-bench, the median of the paired ratios of 3 alternated rounds:
    pp512 +1.1% at the depth 0 and +2.3% at 3072, pp1024 +1.8% at 0 and
    +2.6% at 3072, tg32 +0.0% at 0 and -0.1% at 4096. The plan has no
    effect on a decode of one token.
  - The op profile for the 32 layers: SWIGLU 29.2 against 34.3 ms and
    ffn_down 85.2 against 88.4 ms at 512 tokens, SWIGLU 51.3 against
    61.5 ms and ffn_down 154.3 against 157.7 ms at 1024 tokens.

